9149/files/CC3A6185-DBDF-4572-BE7A-BCF2BE2FD37D.jpg?v=1685743614","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/KeepGoing3fin.jpg?v=1685743615"]],"340027":[null,[]],"340028":[null,[]],"340029":[null,[]],"340030":["This unique top coat was created in 2018 by Katia Ferreira. TC Magic Effect For Magnetic Polishes was created to facilitate the process of achieving a magnetic effect in magnetic polishes. This TC will help you get a great effect even with weaker magnetic polishes. A neodymium magnet is recommended. How to use it:1. Apply two medium coats of the magnetic polish as you would a regular polish, and allow it to dry completely without a top coat. 2. Drip 1 or 2 drops (depending on the length/size of your nail) of this TC and use the brush to spread the TC. 3. Hold the magnet over the nail for 30 seconds to 1 minute. 4. Repeat this process with each nail, one at a time. Seal Glaze When I first thought I needed a Top Coat to get the best out of Purifire (an exclusive PPU polish), I created Seal Glaze. Purifire had a violet jelly base mixed with an extreme red shimmer, and when we applied a Top Coat, the shimmer lost its intensity. So, the idea was to have a Top Coat that could stop the bleeding of the violet pigment - this is its primary use, but not the last. Seal Glaze also protects nail stamping art, but it is the best product for maintaining the magnetic effect, as it can spread after applying a regular top coat. Seal Glaze has a simple formula containing a film-forming agent and a different solvent than nail polish: alcohol. To use it over nail polish, apply a thin coat and let it dry completely (5 to 8 minutes). After being applied, it will cause the polish to look cloudy, but it will clear up as it dries and becomes glossy. We recommend being careful for at least 30 minutes after application. Once dry, you can apply a topcoat. We recommend avoiding formulas that are not 3 or 5-free (for purple or other color polishes that ‘bleed’). If you use it to protect your stamping art, you can use any topcoat. Ingredients: BUTYL ACETATE, ETHYL ACETATE, NITROCELLULOSE, ÁLCOHOL, ISOPROPYL ALCOHOL, ACETYL TRIBUTYL CITRATE, ADIPIC ACID/NEOPENTYL GLYCOL/TRIMELLITIC ANHYDRIDE COPOLYMER, ACRYLATES COPOLYMER",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/rn-image_picker_lib_temp_a7d1e90d-7b54-4676-8370-5ccb67ac3c5b.jpg?v=1775182669","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/rn-image_picker_lib_temp_47e67c94-f874-481f-aa5a-30c5583e4727.jpg?v=1775003672"]],"340031":["Magic Effect For Magnetic Polishes was created to facilitate the process of achieving a magnetic effect in magnetic polishes. Magic Effect will help you get a great effect even with weaker magnetic polishes. A neodymium magnet is recommended. How to use it:1. Apply two medium coats of the magnetic polish as a regular polish and allow it to dry completely without top coat. 2. Drip 1 or 2 drops (depending on the length/size of your nail) of this product and use the brush to spread it. 3. Hold the magnet over the nail for 30 sec to 1 minute. 4. Repeat with each nail once at a time. Ingredients: BUTYL ACETATE, ETHYL ACETATE, NITROCELLULOSE, ÁLCOHOL, ISOPROPYL ALCOHOL, ACETYL TRIBUTYL CITRATE, ADIPIC ACID/NEOPENTYL GLYCOL/TRIMELLITIC ANHYDRIDE COPOLYMER, ACRYLATES COPOLYMER",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/rn-image_picker_lib_temp_26c0cacd-4d57-4e32-926d-a76cc98d6bc8.jpg?v=1741547989"]],"340032":["Magic Effect For Magnetic Polishes was created to facilitate the process of achieving a magnetic effect in magnetic polishes. Magic Effect will help you get a great effect even with weaker magnetic polishes. A neodymium magnet is recommended. How to use it: 1. Apply 2 medium coats of the magnetic polish as a regular polish and allow it to dry without a top coat. 2. Drip 1 or 2 drops (depending on the length/size of your nail) of Magic Effect and use the brush to spread it. 3. Hold the magnet over the nail for 30 to 1 minute. 4.