,"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/IMG-20240605_175302.jpg?v=1717687558","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/IMG-20240605_181147.jpg?v=1717687558","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/IMG-20240605_175337.jpg?v=1717687558","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/IMG-20240605_174943.jpg?v=1717687558","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/IMG-20240605_175224.jpg?v=1717687558"]],"340045":[null,[]],"340046":[null,[]],"340047":["When I first thought I needed a Top Coat to get the best out of Purifire (an exclusive PPU polish), I created Seal Glaze. Purifire had a violet jelly base mixed with an extreme red shimmer, and when we applied a Top Coat, the shimmer lost its intensity. So, the idea was to have a Top Coat that could stop the bleeding of the violet pigment - this is its primary use, but not the last. Seal Glaze also protects nail stamping art, but it is the best product for maintaining the magnetic effect, as it can spread after applying a regular top coat. Seal Glaze has a simple formula containing a film-forming agent and an alcohol solvent, which is different from nail polish. To use it over nail polish, apply a thin coat and let it dry completely (5 to 8 minutes). After being applied, it will cause the polish to look cloudy, but it will clear up as it dries and becomes glossy. We recommend being careful for at least 30 minutes after application. Once dry, you can apply a topcoat. We recommend 3- or 5-free formulas or up (for purple or other color polishes that ‘bleed’). If you use it to protect your stamping art, you can use any topcoat. To use it over nail polish: Apply a very thin coat and let it dry completely. After being applied, it will cause the nail polish to look cloudy, and it will clear up as it dries and becomes glossy. THIS COLOUR WILL BE RESTOCKED. KEEP AN EYE ON THE RESTOCK PAGE FOR UPDATES, OR CLICK ON THE \"NOTIFY ME WHEN BACK IN STOCK\" BUTTON ABOVE. A light blue/green ( hot ) to blue ( warm ) to dark blurple ( cold ) tri thermal nail polish with pink / gold / green shifting iridescent flakes. This polish is heat sensitive and will change from one colour to another at approximately 28°C. Opaque in 2 - 3 coats depending on your application recommended for a glossy finish. ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ***** IMPORTANT INFORMATION ABOUT THERMALS***** Thermal polishes only have a certain shelf life before they expire and they no longer transition ( change colours ). The average shelf life seems to be 6 - 18 months. Many different variables can affect how long they last including how they are stored and the heat/weather etc.Because of this, there is no possible way I can guarantee a certain timeframe. Your polish may last 6 months or it might last years to come, please take note of this when purchasing. I have thermals that still transition well after 4 years so mine do tend to last longer than some other brands. Thermals are still perfectly fine to use even when they no longer transition! ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Product images courtesy of:@icanhazpolish@thepolishblog⁠@lovelylacquerist@mypolishednailz@yyulia_m@cosmeticsanctuary ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Hashtag #emilydemollyaspotinthewoods and tag @emilydemolly for a chance to be featured!Click the link above to see even more photos!",["https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/rn-image_picker_lib_temp_9b527ede-e7b1-4322-a523-ab8950dec871.jpg?v=1775003710","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0542/9968/9149/files/rn-image_picker_lib_temp_47e67c94-f874-481f-aa5a-30c5583e4727.jpg?v=1775003672 https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0920/9752/products/A-spot-edm-7.jpg?v=1678389997","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0920/9752/products/A-spot-edm-10.jpg?v=1678389997","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0920/9752/products/A-spot-edm-8.jpg?v=1678389997","https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0920/9752/products/A-spot-edm-2.jpg?v=1678389997","h